    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`) previously only rolled weekend dates forward to the following Monday. I extended `rollForward` to also skip the fixed public-holiday list.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added a `HOLIDAYS` set containing the five pinned dates: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `rollForward` to loop one day at a time, skipping any Saturday, Sunday, **or** listed holiday, until it lands on a non-holiday weekday. This correctly handles chained cases (e.g. `2026-12-25` is a Friday holiday \u2192 Saturday \u2192 Sunday \u2192 `2026-12-28` which is also a holiday \u2192 `2026-12-29`).\n\nSince `effectiveRegistrationDate` and the callers (`BuildOwner`, `ValidateDailyOwnerLimit`) both funnel through `rollForward`, the derivation and validation paths stay in agreement on the same adjusted day. This mirrors the test's own `toBusinessDay` reference implementation in `AcceptanceBase.java`.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 all tests green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
